hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"994","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: We walked with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when it was late in the night we had our wedding, our eyes were overcome, and nothing woke us up except the heat of the sun, and the man was getting up. He went to his ablution in amazement, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to perform ablution, then he ordered Bilal and he gave the call to prayer, then they prayed the two rak’ahs of dawn, then He ordered him to stand up and perform the Fajr prayer. They said: O Messenger of God, we have neglected. Shall we not repeat it to its time the next day? He said: “Your Lord forbids you from hypocrisy.”"
